.TH GANDER 1 "2025-08-16" "gander 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gander \- render Markdown locally, optionally share it on gander.md
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gander
.RI [ options ]
.IR file.md
.sp
.B gander signup
.RB [ \-email \ Iemail\fR]
.sp
.B gander share
.RB [ \-watch ]
.IR file.md
.sp
.B gander watch
.IR file.md
.sp
.B gander status
.sp
.B gander stop
.RI [\| \fIfile\||\|id\||\|\-\-all\ ||\|\-yes\ ||\|\-non\-interactive\ |\|
.sp
.B gander logs
.RI [\| \fIid\fR\ |
.RB [ \-\-follow | \-\-no\-follow ]]
.sp
.B gander runner
.RB { install | uninstall }
.sp
.B gander remove
.RB [ \-all | "\-pick "\fIshort_id\fR ]
.RB [ \-yes ]
.RB [ \-non\-interactive ]
.IR target
.sp
.B gander list
.sp
.B gander comments
.RI [ file ]
.sp
.B gander mcp
.RB [ install ]
.sp
.B gander skill
.RB [ install ]
.sp
.B gander uninstall
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-\-keep\-config ]
.sp
.B gander manage
.sp
.B gander auth
.IR api_token
.sp
.B gander completion
.RB { bash | zsh }
.sp
.B gander \-\-upgrade
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gander
converts a Markdown file to HTML and opens the result in the default web
browser.
If run with
.BR \-\-watch ","
the preview live\-reloadss in place on save.
After registering with
.B gander signup
the
.BR share ","
.BR watch ","
.BR remove ","
.B list ,
and
.B manage
subcommands upload Markdown to
.RI \(la https://gander.md \(ra
("gander.md") and return short share links.
.SH OPTIONS
These flags apply to the default
.I gander
.BR file " mode."
.TP
.BI \-outfile " string"
Write the rendered HTML to
.I string
instead of opening it in the browser.
.TP
.BR \-watch ", " \-\-watch
Hand the file off to the long\-lived
.B gander _serve
runner daemon; the CLI exits and the daemon owns the watch. Each watch
is reachable at
.BR http://127.0.0.1:7821/w/\fIid\fB?t=\fItoken\fR;
the per\-watch
.I token
is unguessable and stored in
.IR ~/.gander/watches.json .
On every save the rendered HTML hot\-swaps in place and the TOC rebuilds;
scroll position is preserved.
On first
.B \-\-watch
a LaunchAgent (macOS) or
.B systemctl \-\-user
unit (Linux) is installed so the daemon restarts on every login.
May not be combined with
.BR \-outfile .
.IP
.B \-\-foreground
When combined with
.BR \-\-watch ","
run the old blocking watcher in the foreground (the CLI blocks until
.BR Ctrl\-C ;
no runner, no port held across processes). Useful for CI, sandboxes,
or debugging the watcher itself.
.TP
.BR \-upgrade ", " \-\-upgrade
Download and install the latest release, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print help and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Signup"
.TP
.B signup
Open the signup form in your browser, then save the resulting API token
in
.IR ~/.gander/config.json .
The token is required for the other gander.md commands.
.sp
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-email " email
The address to register. Required.
.RE
.SS "Share"
.TP
.B share
Upload
.IR file.md
to gander.md, print the share link, and open it in the browser.
.sp
.RS
.TP
.B \-watch
Continuously push local changes to the remote share until interrupted.
.RE
.SS "Watch"
.TP
.B watch
Shorthand for
.B "share \-\-watch"
\&: upload
.IR file.md
to gander.md and live\-update the remote share on every save. The
share is owned by the runner daemon and survives the CLI's lifetime.
.SS "Status"
.TP
.B status
Print the runner daemon version and uptime, then a table of every
active watch with its runner id, mode, gandermd short id (share
mode), canonical path, age, and URL. Local watches use the
.B "http://127.0.0.1:\fIport\fB/w/\fIid\fB?t=\fItoken\fR"
preview URL; share-mode watches use the gandermd share URL.
.SS "Stop"
.TP
.B stop
Remove a watch from the runner. Accepts the canonical path, a watch
.IR id ","
or
.B \-\-all
to clear everything. The runner returns the list of removed ids and the
CLI prints one
.B stopped
line per removal.
.SS "Logs"
.TP
.B logs
Tail
.IR ~/.gander/runner.log .
On macOS and Linux the file is the daemon's redirected stderr. Pass a
watch
.I id
to filter to a single watch. Pass
.B \-\-no\-follow
to print existing lines and exit; the default is to follow every 500ms.
.SS "Runner"
.TP
.B runner " {install|uninstall}"
Install or remove the LaunchAgent (macOS) /
.B systemctl \-\-user
unit (Linux) that keeps the runner alive across logins. Auto\-installed on the
first
.B \-\-watch
if not present, so this command is mostly for explicit control.
.SS "Remove"
.TP
.B remove
Delete a share previously created by
.BR share .
The argument may be a local file path, an 8\-character
.IR short_id ,
or a
.I https://gander.md/s/<short_id>
URL.
.sp
.RS
.TP
.B \-all
Remove every share matching the argument.
.TP
.BI "\-pick " short_id
When the argument matches more than one share, remove the one with the
given
.IR short_id .
.TP
.B \-yes
Skip the per\-share confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-non\-interactive
Refuse to prompt; require
.B \-all
or
.B \-pick
when the argument is ambiguous.
.RE
.SS "List"
.TP
.B list
Print a table of every share in the user's gander.md account (short id,
file, watch flag, last update, URL).
.SS "Comments"
.TP
.B comments
.RI [ file ]
Print unresolved review comments. With no argument, lists the inbox across
all shares on this machine. With a file, lists comments on that share.
.SS "MCP"
.TP
.B mcp
Run the Gander MCP server on stdio (forked by the agent). Not meant to be
invoked by hand.
.TP
.B mcp install
Merge a Gander MCP entry into OpenCode, Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex
config files. Does not clobber other servers.
.SS "Skill"
.TP
.B skill
.RB [ install ]
Download
.B gandermd/gander-skill
into
.I ~/.gander/skill
and symlink it into the agent skill directories used by OpenCode, Claude
Code, Cursor, and Grok Build. Does not require an API token. Re-running
refreshes the checkout. Refuses to overwrite a destination that is not a
symlink.
.SS "Manage"
.TP
.B manage
Open the gander.md dashboard in your browser. Requires an existing API
token (sign up first). The dashboard shows your shares, rotates your API
token, and lets you attach a password to log in via the web.
.SS "Auth"
.TP
.B auth
Validate and install a new API token, e.g. one you rotated in the
dashboard. Requires an existing API token (sign up first); the command
checks the new token against
.B /api/shares
before overwriting
.IR ~/.gander/config.json .
Email and
.B api_url
are preserved.
.SS "Completion"
.TP
.B completion
Print a shell completion script to standard output.
Takes a single argument naming the shell. Supported:
.RB \(lq bash \(rq
and
.RB \(lq zsh \(rq.
.SS "Uninstall"
.TP
.B uninstall
Tear down everything gander installed on this machine: stop watches and
shut down the runner, remove the LaunchAgent or systemd user unit, strip
MCP
.B gander
entries from OpenCode, Claude, Cursor, and Codex configs, remove skill
symlinks and
.IR ~/.gander/skill ,
and delete the running binary unless it is Homebrew\-managed.
Without
.B \-\-keep\-config
the profile directory
.I ~/.gander
is removed last.
.IP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.B \-\-non\-interactive
is an alias.
Without
.B \-\-yes
on a non\-TTY the command refuses to run.
.IP
.B \-\-keep\-config
Leave
.I ~/.gander
in place so a reinstall can reuse the API token and share map.
.IP
Homebrew\-managed binaries are not deleted; the command prints a hint to
run
.B brew uninstall gander
instead.
.SS "Self\-update"
.TP
.BR \-\-upgrade
Download the latest release binary for the current platform, verify its
checksum, atomically replace the running binary, and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.gander
Profile directory (mode 0700). Holds
.IR config.json ,
.IR watches.json ,
the runner socket, and logs.
.TP
.I ~/.gander/config.json
JSON configuration (mode 0600). Holds the API token, API endpoint,
default flags, and the local map of file path \(-> short id.
A legacy JSON file at
.I ~/.gander
is migrated here on first write or
.BR \-\-watch .
.TP
.I ~/.gander.\fIname\fR
When
.B GANDER_CONFIG=\fIname\fR
is set in the environment, the CLI uses this directory instead of
the default
.IR ~/.gander
(config at
.IR ~/.gander.\fIname\fR/config.json ).
Useful for pointing a single checkout at a local dev or staging instance
without disturbing the prod profile. The legacy
.I ~/.mdp
fallback only applies when
.B GANDER_CONFIG
is unset; named profiles never fall back to
.IR .mdp .
Names must be a single path component (no
.RB \(lq / \(rq,
.RB \(lq \e \(rq,
.RB \(lq . \(rq,
or
.RB \(lq .. \(rq).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (file not found, network failure, ambiguous share,
user rejected a prompt, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
Render a local file and open the preview:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gander README.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Live\-reload the preview while writing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gander \-watch README.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Push the same file to gander.md and open the share link:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gander share README.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Live\-push the file to gander.md on every save (shorthand for
.BR "share \-\-watch" ):
.PP
.RS
.nf
gander watch README.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove a share by short id:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gander remove aBcD1234
.fi
.RE
.PP
Sign up against a local dev gandermd using a separate profile:
.PP
.RS
.nf
GANDER_CONFIG=dev gander signup \-\-email dev@example.com
.fi
.RE
